{
  "label": "concave",
  "explanation": "f(x) = 1/(7/4 + e^x). Let g(x) = 7/4 + e^x > 0. Then f''(x) = e^x (e^x - 7/4) / (g(x))^3. On [-2, -1], e^x ∈ [e^{-2}, e^{-1}] ≈ [0.135, 0.368], which is strictly less than 7/4 = 1.75. Hence e^x - 7/4 < 0 and f''(x) < 0 for all x in [-2, -1]. Therefore the function is concave on this interval (not convex)."
}

{
  "label": "concave",
  "explanation": "For f(x) = 1/(7/4 + e^x) on [-2,-1], f'(x) = -e^x/(7/4 + e^x)^2 and f''(x) = e^x/( (7/4 + e^x)^3 ) * (e^x - 7/4). On this interval e^x ∈ [e^{-2}, e^{-1}] < 7/4, hence e^x - 7/4 < 0 and f''(x) < 0 for all x in [-2,-1]. Therefore the function is concave on the interval."
}

